{
  "_about": "Speech-to-text fixes for the intel rule packs that say \"normalize\": \"stt\" (sizeup/intel/rules.py Normalizer). Data only: \"heard\": \"meant\", words in order, case and punctuation aside, at most 6 words a side. One pass, the longest entry first; a fix is never fixed again. A pack's phrases are tried on the words as transcribed and on the words after these fixes, so an entry can only add a reading: write each rule phrase once, in the spelling on the right-hand side here (\"odor of gas\", \"rollover\", \"en route\", \"2nd alarm\"). Generic vocabulary only: no street names, people, callsigns or anything heard on the air. Keep a sound-alike with its context (\"order of gas\", never \"order\" alone).",
